      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n (i) LOSS OF DEPENDENCY AND FUTURE  PROSPECTS:\n The deceased was working in ALS Testing company as well as Trans Tools Corporation."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "054499b3eac541b4a824398276e2dcd1_236",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As already discussed,\nthe total annual income of the deceased comes to Rs.16,20,715/."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "8964b3c3ee2b40659186fc26774f449d_239",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "23. As per the decision of Hon'ble Supreme Court in National Ins. Co. Ltd. Vs. Pranay Sethi & Ors (2017)\n16 SCC 680, in case of death of a person holding Raghavendra Rao.P vs Royal Sun All Ins Co Ltd on 2 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http:"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "38a2eccf21324487a1fb34cc19e5559b_240",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Temporary job, claimants are entitled for future prospects  32 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25 of 25% if his age is below 50 years."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d161c3c2183c45a8aa47b69a77f81457_241",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This case is also relied upon by the counsel for petitioner."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "55964e6c5f0c42698592c7217d4c3b7f_248",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "If an amount of Rs.4,05,179/ is added to the annual salary of the  33 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25 deceased, then it comes to Rs.20,25,894/."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c7a9c0644fdc4d3cbc42733daae27b88_249",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case the deceased has three dependents."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2b1231e0a2a04e71a489e043f43f2806_255",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n23 total loss of dependency would be Rs.1,75,57,748/\n(Rs.13,50,596/ x 13 = Rs.1,75,57,748/).\n ii) TRANSPORTATION, MEDICAL AND FUNERAL  EXPENSES:"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3bcc44688e7a4116963680e2781e7257_256",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In so far as the funeral and transportation expenses are concerned, the Petitioners have pleaded that they have spent Rs.1,00,000/ towards transportation of dead body,\nfuneral, obsequies and other incidental expenses."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1db551efda524a6db789502fd7f5fdd8_257",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "No documents are produced in this regard."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b164b55e5c9a428a92359a3113e2de55_258",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "However, looking into the facts and circumstances of the case, it is difficulty to maintain bills for transportation of dead body and funeral expenses and hence it would be appropriate to  34 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25 award compe"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5a4784132daf4f73ae87acca30f65d5d_259",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n iii) LOSS OF CONSORTIUM:\n In Magma General Insurance company Limited Vs.\nNanuram (2018) 18 SCC 130, the Hon'ble Apex court has observed \"Consortium\" is a compendious term, which encompasses spousal consortium, parental consortium and fili"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "940a226e046c46f59af6faefe3e41720_260",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The right to consortium would include the company, care, help, comfort, guidance, solace and affection of the deceased, which is a loss to his family."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0153c854d4df4c2f9a718b8773751344_261",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "With respect to a spouse, it would include sexual relations with the deceased spouse\"."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1774c662f9fb41d9baa105e8592646ed_262",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nRaghavendra Rao.P vs Royal Sun All Ins Co Ltd on 2 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/6869582/\n24  24."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "082efe48f65e4530aae3d3bc7e046263_263",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "This observation of the Hon'ble Supreme Court is reaffirmed in United Indian Insurance Company Ltd.\nVs. Satinder Kaur @ Satvinder Kaur and others, (2021)\n11 SCC 780.\n 35 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25  25."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "c4780992043c4745ac8bf19cded304ac_268",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n As mentioned above, the deceased was earning a sum of Rs.20,25,894/ per annum."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9d1f813a16a64c188866a946fce2676c_270",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nSuch being the case, out of this, certainly he would have saved some amount and created estate in favor of the  36 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25 Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "32b699748b8b4157a1376d419dd93b51_280",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per Ex.P.4  37 MVC No.2854 and 2855/2020  SCCH - 25 the deceased and the petitioner in 2855/2020 were standing towards right side of the Car."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "3171c5432bfb4e1ca49d3657a31d41a2_281",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It was their responsibility to show their presence by placing some indicators."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "34f35865bd6240058c153e2d98fc992a_282",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "But the petitioners have not shown that they had placed stones or other indicators to show the stoppage of the vehicle and their presence."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "0f316916c47943d89194fd2c558c8084_283",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, this contention of the respondent No.1 needs to be considered and this Tribunal attributes 10% contributory negligence on the deceased."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "78946fe99eff443bb748bd39a12a03eb_284",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore if the same is deducted the respondents are liable to pay a sum of Rs.1,59,46,020/\nRaghavendra Rao."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5e3a73bb012b402981a525ebca4b82a0_287",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the respondents being the owner and the insurer of the offending vehicle are jointly and severally liable to pay the said compensation to the Petitioners and satisfy the award."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4772893a5eaa4c71a27446fb124d519b_288",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Though the Petitioners have claimed compensation of Rs.4,00,00,000, Petitioners are entitled only for a sum of Rs.1,59,46,020/ with interest @ 6% per annum."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "7a04d781c70e46be8bda7891f746a81f_290",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the petition needs to be allowed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "177ee7fb57114da3bc481e492a3f0156_294",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n In view of above answers to the above issues, this Tribunal proceeds to pass the following:\n ORDER"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "875e5cf114684158be0c0afadbbfbb9e_295",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The petitions in MVC. No.2854/2020 & 2855/2020 are hereby allowed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5591320139d942419f83bbf6d8e2a6d3_296",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nThe Respondents 1 and 2 are jointly and severally liable to pay compensation to the Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "1a62ef1453724059a29eaaebfeae2b26_297",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nHowever, the Respondent No.1 being insurer is liable to indemnify the Respondent No.2 and directed to deposit the compensation amount to the Petitioners within 60 days from today."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5f53fb1e6a864fc0a4f58be88f625a11_298",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nSCCH - 25 The Petitioner in MVC. No.2854/2020 is entitled for total compensation of Rs.1,59,46,020/ (Rupees One Crore Fifty Nine Lakhs Forty Six Thousand and Twenty only) along with interest @ 6% p.a. from the date of filing till the date "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "18c4c5dfacca41ca83abc37e67f2a087_299",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\nOn deposit of the award amount and interest, 20% shall be released to the petitioner No.1 by way of epayment with proper identification and due acknowledgment as per rules."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "ca6ce6dab9ac48558eaaebf6bac8e7c7_300",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Out of the remaining amount, 30% shall be deposited in the name of the Petitioner No.1 for a period of 3 years and 25%\nshall be deposited in the name of Petitioner 2 for a period of 5 years and 25% shall be deposited SCCH - 25 in the name o"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "5fcc6baa9d1f4b13b7f7252a4fccdc9a_302",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Petitioner in MVC. No.2855/2020 is entitled for total compensation of Rs.1,01,000/ (Rupees One Lakh One Thousand only) along with interest @ 6% p.a. from the date of filing till the date of depositing the award amount."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "38e48aa588344726b70fe50646c02345_303",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "On deposit of compensation and interest, entire amount shall be released in favour of the Petitioner by way of epayment and on proper identification and due acknowledgment as per Rules."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "9131295431a44494bcfeec4790255319_304",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Advocate fee is fixed at Rs.1000/ in each case."
    },
